KG42.register("source_edge_archive-ae41c623f5e71d215c0ca14e",{"id":"23-hierarchical_market_structure::v141-c-R008::E::v141-c-R008-E001","paper":"23-hierarchical_market_structure","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","rule_ref":"23-hierarchical_market_structure::v141-c-R008","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R008-E001","source":"pricing.local","target":"coordination.price_signal","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R008-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E011","v141-b-g01-E025"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R008-C001"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"KG31-589dd70d32471060","target":"KG31-e9831a630acebd8d","source_occurrence_id":"23-hierarchical_market_structure::v141-c-R008::V::pricing.local","target_occurrence_id":"23-hierarchical_market_structure::v141-c-R008::V::coordination.price_signal","source_unit_id":"23-hierarchical_market_structure::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","target_unit_id":"23-hierarchical_market_structure::v141-a-M01::coordination.price_signal","omega":{"market_type":"LEM_DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Cross-market price coordination of LA l's WEM bidding using the DNEM market clearing price.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E011","v141-b-g01-E025"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"506b9c049f7a8c3bddecae25326db65dd19d2bf610235bb2d2c3b6c5846a24d8","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","source_definition":"The DNO, as local market coordinator, provides the DNEM market clearing price. Scope: DNEM in the proposed hierarchical WEM-DNEM electricity market.","target_definition":"The DNEM market clearing price is an input to the LA's WEM bidding vector, coordinating its decentralized bidding decision through a local price signal. Scope: Cross-market price coordination of LA l's WEM bidding using the DNEM market clearing price. Condition: LA l plays role “2,” exporting electricity from the DNEM to the WEM.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The DNEM market clearing price is an input to the LA's WEM bidding vector, coordinating its decentralized bidding decision through a local price signal. Scope: Cross-market price coordination of LA l's WEM bidding using the DNEM market clearing price. Condition: LA l plays role “2,” exporting electricity from the DNEM to the WEM.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E011","v141-b-g01-E025"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E011","location":{"location_id":"src-fbc18f73e3-p04-c1r2__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"II-C LAs Objective","anchor_text":"of providing electricity to the distribution network. The LAs bidding vector in the DNEM is given in","equation_id":"(10)-(12)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"R'_l = \\max_{\\psi'_l,P_l^{exp}} \\left[ \\left(\\sum_{o\\in B_l^o} LMP'_o - \\lambda_0\\right) P_l^{exp} \\right] \\tag{10}\n\\underline{\\psi}'_l \\le \\psi'_l \\le \\bar{\\psi}'_l \\tag{11}\n\\rho'_l = \\psi'_l * \\lambda_0. \\tag{12}\nConsidering role “2,” the LA l maximizes the payoff function which is shown in (10), subjected to the constraints on the bidding vector (11). The MCP (\\lambda_0) in the DNEM is the marginal cost of providing electricity to the WEM. The bidding vector of LA l in the WEM is shown in (12)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E025","location":{"location_id":"src-fbc18f73e3-p05-c2r4__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"III. Multilevel Complete Information Game","anchor_text":"p ∂Rl ψ′k+1 = ψ′kl + δ . (46) l ∂ψ′k l 5) The presented game is considered as a dynamic game as the ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The presented game is considered as a dynamic game as the LAs observe the actions of other market participants in one market before updating their bidding strategy in the other. Here, LAs consider the decision made by GENCOs once bidding in the DNEM. Similarly, LAs observe the decision made by microgrids once bidding in the WEM. The bidding vector of LAs in each market is determined based on the awarded dispatch and the price of electricity at the LAs’ bus in the other market. The observability indicator v is a binary parameter, which indicates that the LAs observed the actions of participants in the other market at each iteration. The bidding strategy of market participants update iteratively until the convergence"}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM_DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Cross-market price coordination of LA l's WEM bidding using the DNEM market clearing price.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E011","v141-b-g01-E025"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R008-E001","source":"pricing.local","target":"coordination.price_signal","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R008-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E011","v141-b-g01-E025"]},"paper_scope_note":"The interface between WEM and DNEM is retained; the two LA roles and the 15 MW revenue in Case 1 cannot be treated as general rules for the whole market."}});
